        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "239c0372-a6dd-58fe-960f-ee125a9d5e89",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Bulbophyllum, Bismarckia nobilis\n- Taxonomy: Orchidaceae, flowering plants, genera\n- People: Otto von Bismarck\n\nFacts:\n- Bulbophyllum is the largest genus in the orchid family Orchidaceae.\n- Bulbophyllum has more than 2,000 species and is one of the largest genera of flowering plants, exceeded only by Astragalus.\n- The genus Bismarckia is named for Otto von Bismarck, the first chancellor of the German Empire.\n- The species epithet of Bismarckia nobilis comes from the Latin word for \"noble.\"",
